</math>. Which of the following equations represents this relationship?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b032b7cd-11f6-40fa-b628-4b9e6b868b9d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 18 x plus 13\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>13</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5c2f8ffc-8200-410e-a8a9-56c11e026f00","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals 18 x plus 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f5f115c1-829e-4629-97a1-b4ba75b3997f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus 5 x plus 13\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>13</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5a9368af-0c7d-45db-80f5-7495350a5274","content":"<p><math alttext=\"y equals minus 5 x plus 18\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>18</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5a9368af-0c7d-45db-80f5-7495350a5274"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. A linear relationship can be represented by an equation of the form <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> are constants. It&rsquo;s given in the table that when <math alttext="x equals 0"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, <math alttext="y equals 18"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>18</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="18 equals m left parenthesis 0 right parenthesis plus b"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, or <math alttext="18 equals b"><mrow>
	<mn>18</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>b</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus b"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mi>b</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="y equals m x plus 18"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>18</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. It&rsquo;s also given in the table that when <math alttext="x equals 1"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>1</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, <math alttext="y equals 13"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>13</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="y equals m x plus 18"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mi>m</mi>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>18</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="13 equals m left parenthesis 1 right parenthesis plus 18"><mn>13</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn></math>, or <math alttext="13 equals m plus 18"><mrow>
	<mn>13</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mi>m</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>18</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="negative 5 equals m"><mrow>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>m</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the equation <math alttext="y equals minus 5 x plus 18"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mo>-</mo>
			<mn>5</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>18</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> represents the relationship between <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>.</p>
