    ($SATQ$bd45df49$SATQ$, $SATQ$034cf40e-98a7-4817-a3d0-a76cae0faf07$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Systems of two linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="y equals 3 x plus 9"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="3 y equals 8 x minus 6"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x minus y"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ee25f989-5a06-43fd-9e47-ef931d7564a9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 123\"><mo>-</mo><mn>123</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5fdc404e-4baf-4b1d-be5f-864be737c9f0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 33\"><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"593ea914-5a75-4562-9560-a0ffe95ec48f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8b951377-4786-48df-a9ae-1bd4743c05d7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"57\"><mn>57</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8b951377-4786-48df-a9ae-1bd4743c05d7"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. The first equation in the given system of equations defines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x plus 9"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 x plus 9"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> in the second equation in the given system of equations yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3 left parenthesis 3 x plus 9 right parenthesis equals 8 x minus 6"><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>. Applying the distributive property on the left-hand side of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 x plus 27 equals 8 x minus 6"><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8 x"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus 27 equals negative 6"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="27"><mn>27</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals negative 33"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 33"><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in the first equation of the given system of equations yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 3 left parenthesis negative 33 right parenthesis plus 9"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>,&nbsp;or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals negative 90"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 33"><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 90"><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> into the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x minus y"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 33 minus left parenthesis negative 90 right parenthesis"><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="57"><mn>57</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus y"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x minus y"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x minus y"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>
