<p><br />Choices A, B, and C are incorrect. None of these points are a solution to the given inequality because each point&rsquo;s <em>y</em>-coordinate is greater than the value of&nbsp;<math alttext="minus 4 x plus 4"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;for the point&rsquo;s <em>x</em>-coordinate.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"bf5f80c6","external_id":"4e92e788-6fae-4f7c-a838-84939a7bdd2f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"1b528cea-b234-4931-bc78-07524f32c6eb","uId":"610781bd-312c-4ee8-b488-02beef6bb456","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.E.","skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style='text-align: center;'><math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></math></p>\n<p>Which point (<math><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, <math><mi>y</mi>\n</math>) is a solution to the given inequality in the <math><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>-plane?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"364ba3bf-fb84-42b2-8cdc-152410de4249","content":"<p>(<math><mn>-4</mn>\n</math>, <math><mn>0</mn>\n</math>)</p>"},{"id":"d249192f-1aa4-4ba0-b9d4-92dcc0b663e3","content":"<p>(<math><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, <math><mn>5</mn>\n</math>)</p>"},{"id":"c730111f-f6f1-4955-9274-97f2fd950b77","content":"<p>(<math><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, <math><mn>1</mn>\n</math>)</p>"},{"id":"a9ec40f9-89df-4134-83f5-d09e3c865e83","content":"<p>(<math><mn>2</mn>\n</math>, <math><mn>-1</mn>\n</math>)</p>"}],"keys":["364ba3bf-fb84-42b2-8cdc-152410de4249"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. For a point&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></